## Commands

```bash
flutter pub get
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs   # after changing Riverpod/JSON annotations
dart format .
flutter analyze
flutter test
flutter test test/path/to/file_test.dart --plain-name "test name"   # single test case
```

## Architecture

3-layer Clean Architecture: `Page → Notifier (Riverpod) → UseCase → Repository interface ←→ Entity → Repository impl → DataSource → Model`, with Model → Entity mapping done by a Mapper in the data layer.

- Provider chain: `dataSource → repository → useCase → notifier`.
- Errors use `Either<Failure, T>` + `fold()`, never raw throws.
- State is a `sealed class`; Pages are display-only (`ConsumerWidget`).

## Rules

Detailed rules are in `.claude/rules/` (auto-loaded by path): `presentation.md`, `domain-entities.md`, `data-layer.md`, `tests.md`, `imports.md`, `structure.md` (when the directory tree changes, update `STRUCTURE.md` in the same commit), `git.md`.

## Workflow

- Slash commands: `/check`, `/fix-bug <description>`, `/review-rules`, `/new-feature <name>`.
- Skills: `commit`, `create-pr`, `refactor-to-pattern`, `check-translations`.
- Structure check: `bash .claude/scripts/check_structure.sh` (barrels, relative imports, dependency direction, match with `STRUCTURE.md`).
- Code comments are written in English, kept short, explaining *why* rather than repeating the code.
